            <ArticleTitle>Challenging conventional roles in palliative care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>38-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In October 1991, North Humberside was offered its own in-patient palliative care service. This was a natural development of the existing Macmillan Nurse Service and the hospice day centre. This paper discusses how the role of the nurse practitioner has developed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
